.ds q \N'34'
.TH FISSION @drivermansuffix@ @vendorversion@
.SH NAME
fission \- video driver for framebuffer device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "Section \*qDevice\*q"
.BI "  Identifier \*q"  devname \*q
.B  "  Driver \*qfission\*q"
.BI "  BusID  \*qpci:" bus : dev : func \*q
\ \ ...
.B EndSection
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fission
is an experimental @xservername@ driver for KMS devices.  This driver supports
TrueColor visuals at framebuffer depths of 15, 16, 24, and 30. RandR
1.2 is supported for multi-head configurations. Acceleration is available
through glamor for devices supporting at least OpenGL ES 2.0 or OpenGL 2.1.
If glamor is not enabled, a shadow framebuffer is configured based on the
KMS drivers' preference (unless the framebuffer is 24 bits per pixel, in
which case the shadow framebuffer is always used).
.SH SUPPORTED HARDWARE
The
.B fission
driver supports all hardware where the following is available:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
the Linux DRM KMS ioctls
.IP \(bu 2
dumb object create/map support
.IP \(bu 2
DRM_CAP_ADDFB2_MODIFIERS support
.IP \(bu 2
DRM_CLIENT_CAP_ATOMIC support
.IP \(bu 2
drmCrtcQueueSequence support
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION DETAILS
Please refer to
.BR @xconfigfile@ (@filemansuffix@)
for general configuration details.
This section only covers configuration details specific to this driver.
.PP
For this driver it is not required to specify modes in the screen
section of the config file.  The
.B fission
driver can pick up the currently used video mode from the kernel
driver and will use it if there are no video modes configured.
.PP
For PCI boards you might have to add a BusID line to the Device
section.  See above for a sample line.
.PP
The following driver
.B Options
are supported:
.TP
.BI "Option \*qSWcursor\*q \*q" boolean \*q
Selects software cursor.  The default is
.B off.
.TP
.BI "Option \*qkmsdev\*q \*q" string \*q
The framebuffer device to use. Default: /dev/dri/card0.
.TP
.BI "Option \*qAccelMethod\*q \*q" string \*q
One of \*qglamor\*q or \*qsoft2d\*q.  Default: glamor.
.TP
.BI "Option \*qVariableRefresh\*q \*q" boolean \*q
Enables support for enabling variable refresh on the Screen's CRTCs
when an suitable application is flipping via the Present extension.
.sp 2
The default is
.B off.
.sp 2
Not supported on soft2d.
.TP
.BI "Option \*qCompositing\*q \*q" boolean \*q
Compose redirected windows into a separate pair of mode-sized framebuffers
for each CRTC, with independent page flips. Requires GLAMOR, PageFlip and
the Composite extension. Enabled by default on primary GPU screens when
those requirements are met.
.sp 2
The server owns the compositor selection while Compositing is enabled.
Opaque fullscreen PRESENT windows may scan out directly on their monitor.
Rotated or scaled outputs and outputs with a software cursor are composited.
VariableRefresh follows the directly scanned out window on each CRTC.
.sp 2
The server's
.B -fakescreenfps
option controls the presentation rate for off-screen and fully covered
windows. Hardware-backed screens default to 1 frame per second for these
windows. Presentation by the same client to visible windows continues at
the normal rate.
.TP
